WEBVTT

00:05:58.916 --> 00:06:01.276
They didn't say, "I made a lot of money"

00:06:01.316 --> 00:06:03.916
or "I won some big awards."

00:06:03.916 --> 00:06:05.836
They said,

00:06:05.836 --> 00:06:07.236
"I was a good mentor,"

00:06:07.236 --> 00:06:08.836
"I was a good friend,"

00:06:08.836 --> 00:06:10.996
"I raised healthy kids,"

00:06:11.036 --> 00:06:12.636
"I was a good partner."

00:06:13.676 --> 00:06:14.836
And so what we find

00:06:14.876 --> 00:06:17.356
is that what seems to mean
the most to people

00:06:17.396 --> 00:06:19.556
when they get to the end of their lives

00:06:19.556 --> 00:06:23.716
is the strength and the warmth
of their connections to others.

00:06:25.076 --> 00:06:27.996
So then the question comes up, well,

00:06:27.996 --> 00:06:32.356
which types of relationships
support our well-being?